  "name": "Eckau",
  "date": "19 July 1812",
  "campaign": "russia-1812",
  "summary": "Macdonald's X Corps opened its campaign against Riga by driving the Russians out of Courland. At Eckau, south of Riga, Grawert's Prussians met the detachment Essen had sent out under Löwis: artillery and dragoons fixed it in front while Kleist's infantry came in from the east in the evening, and the Russians fell back on Riga.",
