    {
      "id": "eckau-lowis",
      "nationId": "russia",
      "name": "Löwis's Detachment",
      "formation": "From the Riga garrison (Essen)",
      "side": "Russian",
      "summary": "Depot battalions and Cossacks sent out from Riga to hold the line of the Eckau. They held the manor and the crossing through the day until outflanked, and lost several hundred men, many taken, before falling back to Riga.",
      "notes": [
        "The depot (second) battalions of three Jäger regiments, two each, with a Cossack regiment and a battery. Strengths differ: one account gives the detachment 2,000 men, another 3,000–4,000 and ten guns; the battalions are Small.",
        "On its own it has none of the list's Infantry Brigades, which shows as a historical departure.",
        "A staff-captain of the 4th Jäger was killed here; the church records of Gross-Eckau name him.",
        "Commanders are at Staff Rating 8, the default for historical forces; but 1 of the 2 brigade commanders at 7, as the list rates at most half of them higher."
